@startuml SD_CompareScenarios
title UC-W05 - Compare What-if Scenarios
hide footbox
autonumber

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #42566B
  LifeLineBorderColor #8295A8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #D8EAFE
  ParticipantBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  GroupBorderColor #8295A8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
}

actor Operator as OP
boundary "Scenario Comparison UI" as UI
control "SimulationController" as C
control "ScenarioComparisonService" as CS
entity "SimulationRunRepository" as RR

OP -> UI: Open Compare Scenarios
UI -> C: listCompletedRuns()
C -> RR: findCompletedRuns()
RR --> C: Run summaries + baseline option
C --> UI: Available comparison targets

OP -> UI: Select Run A and Run B or baseline
UI -> C: compare(runAId, runBId | baseline)
C -> RR: loadResultsAndMetadata(selection)
RR --> C: Results, recommendation outcomes, metric schema,\nsnapshots, assumptions and time horizons

alt Run missing, failed or not completed
  C --> UI: Comparison unavailable with reason
  UI --> OP: Select another completed run
else Runs available
  C -> CS: assessComparability(runA, runB)
  CS -> CS: Match metric names, definitions and units
  CS -> CS: Detect snapshot, freshness,\nassumption and horizon differences

  alt No meaningful common measure
    CS --> C: Incompatible measures + reasons
    C --> UI: Reject misleading comparison
    UI --> OP: Explain incompatibility
  else Common measures available
    CS -> CS: Compare only common measures
    CS -> CS: Calculate deltas for service capacity, parking,\nvehicles, congestion, delay and projected revenue
    CS -> CS: Compare recommendation outcomes and expected effects
    CS --> C: Comparable values, outcomes, deltas and warnings
    C --> UI: Render side-by-side comparison
    UI --> OP: Show results and recommendation outcomes with\nbaseline context, assumptions and warnings
  end
end

note over C,RR
Comparison is read-only. It does not modify either run,
its recommendations or the live network.
end note
@enduml
